 may manifest as diarrhea or constipation. Additionally, IBS can be associated with various food intolerances, further complicating the management of the condition.\",4\r\n9786,ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FODMAP,\"Foods high in FODMAPs include certain dairy products, fruits, vegetables, and grains that can lead to gastrointestinal discomfort for sensitive individuals.\",2\r\n8353,DIETAS HIPOPROTEICAS,Dietas diseñadas para reducir la ingesta de proteínas y así disminuir las concentraciones de urea en sangre y el síndrome urémico en pacientes con enfermedad renal,3\r\n9530,ALCACHOFA,\"Alcachofa is a vegetable recognized for its nutritional properties, particularly its content of fructans, which may trigger symptoms in individuals with FODMAP intolerance. Additionally, it contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This combination of characteristics makes alcachofa a noteworthy food item for those managing dietary sensitivities.\",1\r\n9782,CEBOLLINO,Cebollino is a food item that contains fructans and can affect those with FODMAP intolerance.,1\r\n9536,ESPÁRRAGO,\"Espárrago is a vegetable that is recognized for its nutritional properties. It contains fructans, which may trigger symptoms in individuals who are sensitive to FODMAPs. Additionally, Espárrago has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This combination of characteristics makes Espárrago a noteworthy food item, particularly for those managing dietary sensitivities.\",1\r\n9780,RAÍZ DE ACHICORIA,Raíz de achicoria is a food item that is high in fructans and can contribute to FODMAP-related digestive symptoms.,1\r\n9546,PLÁTANO,\"Plátano is a type of banana, recognized as a fruit that is rich in dietary fiber. It is a food item that can contain varying levels of FODMAPs, which may impact individuals who are sensitive to these compounds. Additionally, Plátano contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams.\",1\r\n9983,FOOD INTOLE