oimmune response associated with celiac disease.\",1\r\n8445,FOOD INTOLERANCES,Food intolerances refer to adverse reactions to specific foods that do not engage the immune system. These intolerances often require individuals to make dietary modifications to avoid discomfort and other related symptoms.,1\r\n11535,ALIMENTOS SIN FOSFATOS AÑADIDOS,\"Foods labeled \"\"without added phosphates\"\" are becoming available, which is beneficial for phosphorus management.\",1\r\n9787,ALTERNATIVAS,Alternatives to high FODMAP foods are suggested to ensure a nutritionally adequate diet while avoiding foods that may cause symptoms.,1\r\n8567,FÁRMACOS COMERCIALIZADOS,\"Marketed drugs refer to pharmaceutical products that are available for sale and used in the treatment of various conditions, including obesity.\",1\r\n9981,IBS-D,\"Irritable Bowel Syndrome with Diarrhea, a gastrointestinal disorder characterized by abdominal pain and altered bowel habits.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3044,PACIENTE,DIETA,\"The PACIENTE must adhere to a specific DIETA to effectively manage their diabetes and insulin requirements. This DIETA is tailored to meet the individual nutritional needs of the patients, ensuring that they receive the appropriate dietary support necessary for their health management.\",611\r\n2715,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FODMAP,\"FODMAPs can affect patients receiving nutrición enteral, potentially leading to diarrhea\",357\r\n1173,MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA,DIETA,The manual provides guidelines for creating therapeutic diets for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia,278\r\n754,NUTRICIÓN,DIETA,Nutrition is the foundation for creating a diet that meets the needs of individuals with specific health conditions,274\r\n1577,DIABETES MELLITUS,DIETA,Las dietas son esenciales para el control de la diabetes mellitus y la regulación de la glucosa en sangre,229\r\n780,NUTRICIÓN,SII,Nutritional support may be necessary for pati